{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome","id":401553,"title":"Vigil for Rome","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-11T01:07:35-08:00","id":401553,"title":"Vigil for Rome","content":"Another thread got me thinking about this again. I wasn't a fan of the canon version of the Aves Minerva in Paterfamilias. Because while &quot;Ancient Roman Hunters&quot; is a cool hook for uncovering ancient mysteries in a modern setting - in an 4th Century Roman setting, they need to be more distinct than than, especially if other Compacts and Conspiracies are in play.<br /> <br /> So, in theory, my idea for Aves Minerva is to make them &quot;the Union&quot; of the era. They wield no mystical Endowments, but are essentially a self-defense network of common people out of the Aventine (which is also where organized crime is at its strongest in the city). Their impact on Hunter lore comes not from great secrets or powers they protected, but from heroic deeds alone.<br /> <br /> That being the case I have a list of groups, I can theoretically break into 5 Compacts and 5 Conspiracies.<br /> <br /> 5 Compacts:<br /> - <b>Aves Minerva</b> (see above)<br /> - <b>Fraternitas Amissa</b> (a for profit network of couriers and guards for travel through the dark wilderness between cities)<br /> - <b>Shoftim</b> (protectors of the dispersing Children of Judea, they may once have been a Conspiracy, but their Holy Psalms and centralized leadership were lost with the Second Temple)<br /> -???<br /> -???<br /> <br /> 5 Conspiracies<br /> - <b>Aegis Kai Doru</b> (Orphic Mystery Cult reforming via Christian members in the shadow of Constantinople)<br /> - <b>Collegia Chironos</b> (trade network of educated Greek slaves, with secret medical knowledge far beyond the time, drawn from their worshiped brands)<br /> - <b>Cult of the Phoenix</b> (spread through what is now Parthia in the days of Achaemanid rule of Egypt; they marry Ancient Egyptian Alchemy to Zoroastrian Sacred Haoma)<br /> - <b>Lux Mithrae</b> (an order within the Roman Legions who fight the darkness for the Empire and for Mithras. They use Sacramental Bull's blood in their Endowments [steal the Red Rites from Aves Minerva])<br /> - ???<br /> <br /> So as you can see, there are 3 groups I'm uncertain on. Any of these can be Compacts or Conspiracies depending on how I model them and their Endowments.<br /> <br /> - <b>Bacchantes</b> (matriarchal mad revelers that Livy wrote on - of course in reality Livy's telling is very suspect, but in the World of Darkness it's fair game. As a Compact they'd essentially be the era's Ashwood Abbey; but as a Conspiracy, they'd be a Mystery Cult with some real mojo via their mad ecstasies)<br /> - <b>Noctis Vigiles</b> (Christian Hunters... I'm a bit unsure on their SPECIFIC ideology - in an earlier century I'd focus on eschatological fervor, but we're post Nicea at this point, so there's much more organized clerical and doctrinal authority for them to draw on and answer to; they're also not the underclass like Lancea et Sanctum in Requiem for Rome, because other than the &quot;Apostate&quot; calling himself Caesar, mortal Christians are in their political ascendancy, and their faith commands the Eastern half of the Empire unchallenged from Constantinople)<br /> - <b><a href=\"https://nottsvalin.files.wordpress.com/2008/02/wunjo.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">[Wunjo]</a> </b>(link goes to a literal image of the rune &quot;wunjo&quot; that is their name - a Germanic pagan group that seeks out monsters to fight for glory and honor. I'm leaning toward making them Tier 2, but given them runes with some mystic oomf would also make sense)<br /> <br /> Thoughts on how to divy up those last 3? Ideas to further flesh them out (Noctis Vigiles is obviously the most in need - the era needs Christian Hunters, but I haven't decided on more distinct themes for them)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T05:39:55-08:00","id":401776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome#post401553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thoughts on how to divy up those last 3? Ideas to further flesh them out (Noctis Vigiles is obviously the most in need - the era needs Christian Hunters, but I haven't decided on more distinct themes for them)?</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Wunjo</b> I'd definately make Tier 2; I would go so far as to say the wunjo don't have the runes, they just know people outside the compact who are willing to provide them.<br /> <br /> <b>Noctis Vigiles</b>. Hmmm, I'm not to sure about the history so this might not fit the time period. But maybe an Endowment that's primarally focused on magic resistance and undo magical effects, with a sideline in the ability to assimilate other people's magic and make it their own.<br /> <br /> The idea being that as Christianity eclipsed paganism pagan magics stop working, and as Christianity syncretised elements of other faith they're going to syncretise elements of other magic into their own. A loss for human diversity when they do it to the Wunjo, but a good thing when they do it to vampires.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if it should be ritualised or if it should be a passive power of faith thing. But either way it should stop working for reasons at some point before neo-paganism, Buddhism, athiesm, etc start making inroads into previously Christian nations. And possibly before the MM was founded, if only to explain why it hasn't shown up in the cannon books.<br /> <br /> <b>Bacchantes</b>. I'd make them a Conspiracy. If only because we already have an Abbey without magic and this will seperate the two. Plus there's been a lot of work to diversify the Abby from just drug fueled orgies. Livy's portrayal would undo that diversification so magic might help round them out a bit and give them reasons and motives to be terrible people.<br /> <br /> I know that makes two Conspiracies. But I know that the Noctis Vigiles would fit nicely into a single 1-5 Endowment merit so you could cheat a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome#post401553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their impact on Hunter lore comes not from great secrets or powers they protected, but from heroic deeds alone.</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not really sure how this works. Surely there's hundreds of non-Endowed ordinary people with heroic deeds. What makes them stand out?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T06:14:00-08:00","id":401797,"title":"","content":"May I ask why the Lux Mithrae have the Endowments of the Aves Minerva? I mean, we do have them and their Endowments in canon. It feels a little weird with all kind of other things that there are in the books already, especially since it mixes together with the history of the Cainte Heresy. (while I could see the Lux Mithrae tied to vampires and blood magic, given the background from Mythologies and Requiem for Rome, but I just wonder what one gain from this change)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-11T11:48:00-08:00","id":402194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=401797#post401797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">May I ask why the Lux Mithrae have the Endowments of the Aves Minerva? I mean, we do have them and their Endowments in canon. It feels a little weird with all kind of other things that there are in the books already, especially since it mixes together with the history of the Cainte Heresy. (while I could see the Lux Mithrae tied to vampires and blood magic, given the background from Mythologies and Requiem for Rome, but I just wonder what one gain from this change)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Because as I said, canon Aves Minerva is a generic &quot;Ancient Roman Hunters&quot; group with no distinct theme beyond that - which doesn't work if you have a setting with different groups of Ancient Roman Hunters. So I made them a &quot;Union&quot; style Compact, which is how the earlier HtV books described them anyway.<br /> <br /> And the Red Rites become a lot more interesting when they have some cultural weight behind them - in this case, Mithraism with consecrated bull's blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T02:42:20-08:00","id":403131,"title":"","content":"For the Christian compact you could base it off the practice of seeking martyrdom, now that the Roman State isn't persecuting Christians. There was an extreme practice among some Christians of provoking others (presumably non-christians) into attacking you in order to die a martyr, so it's not any more extreme than real life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T06:03:01-08:00","id":403229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=402194#post402194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Because as I said, canon Aves Minerva is a generic &quot;Ancient Roman Hunters&quot; group with no distinct theme beyond that - which doesn't work if you have a setting with different groups of Ancient Roman Hunters. So I made them a &quot;Union&quot; style Compact, which is how the earlier HtV books described them anyway.<br /> <br /> And the Red Rites become a lot more interesting when they have some cultural weight behind them - in this case, Mithraism with consecrated bull's blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>well, I actually felt that the info given from Petrafamila and Night Stalkers was enough for me as far as it is about the Aves Minerva- but it may be just me. It may also be because I'm kinda disapointed that the Lux Mithrae don't get their own, shiny Endowments- but again, it may because of a personal taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T15:56:14-08:00","id":403792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=403229#post403229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> well, I actually felt that the info given from Petrafamila and Night Stalkers was enough for me as far as it is about the Aves Minerva- but it may be just me. It may also be because I'm kinda disapointed that the Lux Mithrae don't get their own, shiny Endowments- but again, it may because of a personal taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've just never understood why Aves Minerva would have mystic blood rites in the first place. it doesn't make any cultural or metaphysical sense to me. I'll expand on them for Lux Mithrae, but at least with them - the sacred blood of the bull of Mithras actually has some meaning.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T16:10:46-08:00","id":403811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=401776#post401776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know that makes two Conspiracies. But I know that the Noctis Vigiles would fit nicely into a single 1-5 Endowment merit so you could cheat a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually works ok, because I thought of another Compact. The <b>Mos Maiorum</b> are a small network of Patricians dedicated to maintaining their families' honor by eliminating their vampiric (or otherwise undying) relatives.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not really sure how this works. Surely there's hundreds of non-Endowed ordinary people with heroic deeds. What makes them stand out? </div> </div> </div>Because someone wrote about their heroic deeds/sacrifice, and that writing happened to survive in Hunter circles. Same reason any given ancient world writing/event gets remembered vs. those that are forgotten.<br /> <br /> Also the Conspiracies are better at keeping themselves secret by their very nature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T16:23:20-08:00","id":403837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=403131#post403131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Christian compact you could base it off the practice of seeking martyrdom, now that the Roman State isn't persecuting Christians. There was an extreme practice among some Christians of provoking others (presumably non-christians) into attacking you in order to die a martyr, so it's not any more extreme than real life.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Perfect! I'll use this for a Christian Compact to round out a 6/6 split, while for a Christian Conspiracy (commanded from Constantinople - the Bishop of Rome not yet being the single established voice of God of Earth for the Western Church), I'll focus on breaking the power of Gnostic sorcerers and Pagan cults to save souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-12T18:13:39-08:00","id":403946,"title":"","content":"Two Christian groups.<br /> <br /> Compact: <b>Vox M\u00e1rtyom</b> (nicknamed the &quot;Agonistici&quot;)<br /> <br /> Conspiracy:<b> Ieros Dromos </b>(named for the &quot;Sacred Way&quot; where according to legend Simon Magus fell breaking his leg when he attempted to fly proving his divinity)<br /> <br /> The Vox Martyom's clinging to martydom as a necessary Christian virtue will eventually get them targeted as a heresy themselves, but at the moment the Ieros Dromos are mainly focused on Gnostic Witches and those Pagan horrors that build cults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T00:43:54-08:00","id":404187,"title":"","content":"&quot;Agonistici&quot; comes from Agony and not Agnostic right?<br /> <br /> Anyway, looks good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T00:57:18-08:00","id":404190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=404187#post404187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Agonistici&quot; comes from Agony and not Agnostic right?<br /> <br /> Anyway, looks good <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> &quot;Agon&quot; means &quot;struggle&quot;, so yeah, no relation to &quot;agnostic&quot; which comes from &quot;gnosis&quot; (i.e. &quot;does not know&quot;).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T19:08:23-08:00","id":405388,"title":"","content":"Do you think that there would be something like the equivlent of vascu but for the roman goverment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1381-herkles","name":"herkles","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-13T20:40:56-08:00","id":405433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>herkles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=405388#post405388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think that there would be something like the equivlent of vascu but for the roman goverment?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really. VASCU is very rooted in modern genre tropes that rose out of the Victorian/Edwardian period. Furthermore, Roman murder case prosecution were handled by private suit (i.e. the family of the victim, not the state, brought charges before the court, called witnesses, etc). So there were no governmental investigative bodies.<br /> <br /> Aves Minerva is likely to act on a family's behalf with a Slasher/supernatural killing - if it gets to a point that PUBLIC ORDER is threatened, Lux Mithrae may step in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-13-2015, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-17T02:45:28-08:00","id":408723,"title":"","content":"So with Ieros Dromos' Endowments, I'm imagining powers closer in effect to Goetic Gospels than to Benedictions, though without the heretical Goetic angle. My thinking is that the Knights of Saint George of course came with Richard on the Third Crusade, and in Asia Minor discovered the lost miracles of Ieros Dromos, which they'd claim to understand better than their predecessors thanks to the Revelations of the Faceless Angels (hence the different, Goetic, results in their hands).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:29:34-08:00","id":411129,"title":"","content":"So i've hacked at my setting with Occam's Razor to make it more manageable and thematic. I think it's fitting that a smaller-scale world would have less major Hunter organizations focused on than the modern scale Western setting of the HtV core, so here's my idea as it stands now. Six orgs TOTAL with full write-ups.<br /> <br /> Tier 2<br /> <b>Aves Minerva</b> - Plebian (and Freemen) defenders of the streets of Rome<br /> <b>Mos Maiorum</b> - Patricians upholding their family honor against the blight of undeath<br /> <b>Vox Martyom</b> - Fervent Christians seeking martyrdom before the unholy as their path to salvation<br /> <br /> Tier 3<br /> <b>Collegia Chironos</b> - Secret cult made up primarily of educated Greek slaves, seeking knowledge medical and mystical of unknown. [Endowments in this era is &quot;The Sign&quot;, which appears as a brand somewhere on the flesh of the cultist, and grants powers in a system most like the tiers of Teleinformation. These powers grant healing abilities and other stranger biological effects. At the highest tier, one can TEMPORARILY wield or grant a Dread Power via the body part of a monster. Permanent Thaumatechnology is still centuries of research away]<br /> <b>Ieros Dromos</b> - Nicean Christian order answerable to Constantinople breaking the power of Gnostic witches and the cults of pagan horrors to save the souls of the masses<br /> <b>Lux Mithrae</b> - Order of holy warriors of Mithras in the Roman Legions, wielding the consecrated blood of the bull in service to the Empire<br /> <br /> <br /> THEN, you get a page sized spread on &quot;other hunter orders in the Ancient Roman world&quot;. This includes the Shoftim and [Wunjo], which are described with some cultural and historic info, but for mechanics the reader is recommended to reskin Aves Minerva and Vox Martyom respectively, as the two Compacts are respectively Community-Defenders (only Jewish rather than Roman pagan) and Self-Destructive Conflict-Seekers (only Germanic Pagan instead of Christian).<br /> <br /> And you get on the same page what Aegis Kai Doru and the Cult of the Phoenix are up to in the era - including some notes on how in the absence of modern narcotics, the Ascending Ones use the rare sacred plant <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haoma\" target=\"_blank\">Haoma</a> as the catalyst of their Elixers. This herb will be lost by the modern day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Then the Bacchantes get included in the antagonist section as a supernatural cult.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Fraternitas Amissa kind of get left out in the cold on this one, but overall I think this works a lot better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-18T23:51:26-08:00","id":411139,"title":"","content":"You may wish to look at<a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/144754/Eagle-Eyes--A-World-of-Adventure-for-Fate-Core?affiliate_id=24139\" target=\"_blank\"><i> Eagle Eyes</i></a>; it's a FATE game that released today (and it's pay-what-you-want!) about the Senate's secret service dedicated to rooting out conspiracies against the Republic. It's also damn good, and definitely worthy inspiration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-19T10:48:51-08:00","id":411755,"title":"","content":"It all looks good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/401553-vigil-for-rome?p=411129#post411129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">including some notes on how in the absence of modern narcotics, the Ascending Ones use the rare sacred plant <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haoma\" target=\"_blank\">Haoma</a> as the catalyst of their Elixers. This herb will be lost by the modern day.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the modern day the AO use many different catalysts, I don't see why that should be different in the acient world.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}